  "id": "negative-adaptation",
  "term": "negative adaptation",
  "definition": "Negative adaptation is a learning-related neural effect in which prior exposure to a stimulus is followed by a reduced brain response to that stimulus later. In this source, it was found for stimuli that were attended but made unreportable by masking.",
